# The CENTRE's healing machine: one tile of the bank along the back wall.
#
# Y is up, +Z is north, one world unit is one map tile. The lowest vertex sits
# on y = 0 and the model is centred on x = 0 and z = 0, so the game places it
# by its feet.
#
# Faces are wound so that (c - a) x (b - a) points out of the solid, which is
# what tools/obj2cpp.py bakes as the face normal. Get it backwards and the
# model still draws, it just goes flat ambient dark.
#
# A cabinet with a lit panel across its front and a tray of ball slots on
# top. 1.15 units, so the bank clears the desk in front of it and reads as
# two rows of fittings rather than one lumpy one.
#
# 16 triangles. There are five of these in the room, which is the whole
# reason the tray is a slab with a coloured top rather than three domes:
# domes at this size are four pixels each and cost twelve triangles apiece.

mtllib machine.mtl

# the cabinet
v -0.52 0.00 -0.52
v  0.52 0.00 -0.52
v  0.52 0.00  0.52
v -0.52 0.00  0.52
v -0.52 1.15 -0.52
v  0.52 1.15 -0.52
v  0.52 1.15  0.52
v -0.52 1.15  0.52

# the tray of slots, sitting on top and set back
v -0.40 1.15 -0.30
v  0.40 1.15 -0.30
v  0.40 1.15  0.30
v -0.40 1.15  0.30
v -0.40 1.32 -0.30
v  0.40 1.32 -0.30
v  0.40 1.32  0.30
v -0.40 1.32  0.30

usemtl machine_body
f 5 6 7 8
f 2 3 7 6
f 4 1 5 8

usemtl machine_panel
f 1 2 6 5

usemtl machine_slots
f 13 14 15 16

usemtl machine_tray
f 9 10 14 13
